# busybox init stays PID 1; /init has already done the mounts and USB gadget
# setup. OpenRC starts and supervises every service (etc/init.d,
# etc/runlevels/default; docs/features/services.md). This file keeps only
# what must not depend on OpenRC, and runs it.
#
# The shell gets root's home and session bus (root-session-bus) the way a
# desktop login would. The passwordless USB recovery shell: started by init
# itself, whatever happens to OpenRC.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'export HOME=/root XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/0 DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/run/user/0/bus; exec /usr/sbin/telnetd -F -b 172.16.42.1 -l /bin/sh'
# OpenRC: its own sysinit step (it creates /run/openrc and /run/lock and
# builds the dependency tree; the sysinit and boot runlevels are empty,
# /init does that work), then the default runlevel, also if that step
# failed. ::once, not ::wait: a service that hangs must not hold back the
# telnetd line above.
::once:/bin/sh -c '/sbin/openrc sysinit; exec /sbin/openrc default'
# A/B slot: mark boot_a successful once this boot has lasted 30 s, as
# Android's boot_control HAL did, so abl stops counting retries down (it
# would mark the slot unbootable after 7 boots). A build that dies earlier
# keeps counting and ends in fastboot. Logs to syslog and
# /run/chef/log/abslot.log.
::once:/bin/sh -c 'sleep 30; exec /usr/bin/abslot mark-successful >/dev/null'
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
# chef-state first (last RTC offset, chronyd stopped so its drift file is
# written, last magnetometer bias; it stops chronyd, powerd, sensord and
# the timekeeper through OpenRC), bounded so it cannot hold up the rest;
# then the syslogd ring, with the lines of that stop, onto
# /data/v1/log/syslog-<seq> (syslogd still runs: init signals every process
# only after these lines; bounded too); then OpenRC stops every other
# service in reverse dependency order, modem-up's clean modem stop included,
# while /data is still mounted (bounded: modem-up's stop takes about 11 s,
# the kernel's 10 s wait for a shutdown ack the modem never sends, and the
# whole step 14.2 s live; 30 s covers modem-up's TERM 15 s and KILL 2 s plus
# one other service stuck for its TERM 5 s and KILL 2 s and the quick stops
# of the rest; init reaps at once while it runs these lines, so a stop costs
# only its own time); then any supervisor openrc shutdown left (it did not
# finish) is stopped, so nothing respawns what chef-storage's sweep stops
# next; then chef-storage makes /data read-only and detaches it.
::shutdown:/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 5 /usr/bin/chef-state shutdown
::shutdown:/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 3 /usr/bin/chef-state log-save
::shutdown:/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 30 /sbin/openrc shutdown
::shutdown:/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 10 /usr/bin/chef-stop-supervisors
::shutdown:/usr/bin/chef-storage shutdown
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
# Before it runs ::restart, init runs every ::shutdown line above (which
# save the ring and stop every OpenRC service) and kills every process, so
# there is no log-save or openrc shutdown here; the new init's ::once line
# starts the services again.
::restart:/bin/sh -c '/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 5 /usr/bin/chef-state shutdown; /usr/bin/chef-storage shutdown; exec /sbin/init'
